---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms | HUMANITY"
  description="Draft terms and responsible-use notice for the HUMANITY public event research interface."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="border-b border-humanity-border pb-7">
      <p class="eyebrow">Transparency</p>
      <h1 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">
        Terms of use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted">
        Draft for legal review · Not a final legal agreement
      </p>
    </header>
    <div
      class="prose-copy max-w-3xl space-y-7 py-8 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Research information, not a complete record
        </h2><p class="mt-3">
          HUMANITY is a developing public-interest interface to selected
          source-linked event records. It is not a comprehensive news service,
          official incident database, emergency alert, or substitute for reading
          original reporting. A published record does not establish every claim
          as true; an absent record does not establish that an event did not
          occur.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Uncertainty and availability
        </h2><p class="mt-3">
          Records may be delayed, incomplete, disputed, revised, or temporarily
          unavailable. The project does not promise continuous availability, a
          particular update schedule, error-free data, or fitness for a specific
          decision. Review source links and assess uncertainty independently.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Third-party material
        </h2><p class="mt-3">
          Source names, article titles, links, excerpts, images, and other
          third-party content remain subject to their owners' terms. A citation
          or link is not a license. The repository's MIT license applies to
          software, not external reporting or data. No permission to copy, sell,
          or redistribute third-party material is granted; see the <a
            class="link"
            href="/source-rights">source-rights disclosure</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold text-humanity-text">
          Responsible use and contact
        </h2><p class="mt-3">
          Do not use an incomplete or uncertain record as the sole basis for a
          high-impact decision about an individual or community. Report factual
          or attribution concerns through the <a
            class="link"
            href="https://github.com/asdfhgds/humanity/issues"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">public issue tracker</a
          >, without including sensitive personal information.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <p
      class="border-t border-humanity-border pt-5 text-xs text-humanity-textMuted"
    >
      This draft must be adapted by qualified counsel before being presented as
      binding terms or relied on for a commercial service.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
